teAction()\" (if \"isValidSignature()\" is also skipped) will revert, since the order hash and tokenOut will not be set.GPv2Settlement ensures that signatures for the same orderHash (and hence messageHash) cannot be replayed. No need to again check for replay attacks here.The swapFee, if non-zero is always paid to the initiator, also if the Account owner is the signer. While suboptimal, \"isValidSignature()\" is a view only function so we can't check who is the actual signer. The Account owner can always sign with the fee set to 0.","params":{"initiatorData":"The encoded remaining initiator parameters."}},"changeGuardian(address)":{"params":{"guardian_":"The address of the new guardian."}},"constructor":{"params":{"arcadiaFactory":"The contract address of the Arcadia Factory.","flashLoanRouter":"The contract address of the flash-loan router.","hooksTrampoline":"The contract address of the hooks trampoline.","owner_":"The address of the Owner."}},"executeAction(bytes)":{"params":{"callBackData":"A bytes object containing callBack data."},"returns":{"depositData":"A struct with the data to deposit the bought tokens in the account."}},"flashLoanAndCallBack(address,address,uint256,bytes)":{"details":"Only one account at a time can be included per \"flashLoanAndSettle()\"The check that the solver passed the correct input parameters is done via the signature validation in \"beforeSwap()\". Both the order parameters (tokenIn_ and amountIn_) as the account_ are included in the messageHash. If a malicious solver modifies the input parameters, the initiator signature will no longer be valid.","params":{"account_":"The contract address of the account.","amountIn_":"The amount of tokenIn to swap.","callBackData":"The calldata to be passed back to the flash-loan router.","tokenIn_":"The contract address of the token to swap from."}},"isValidSignature(bytes32,bytes)":{"details":"There is no guarantee the solver includes a call to \"isValidSignature()\". A malicious solver could modify the signature, skipping the check that the orderHash is correct. If \"isValidSignature()\" would be skipped, the transaction will revert during \"executeAction()\".GPv2Settlement ensures that signatures for the same orderHash (and hence messageHash) cannot be replayed. No need to again check for replay attacks here.","params":{"orderHash_":"Hash of the CoW Swap order.","signature":"Initiator signature encoded as (bytes32 r, bytes32 s, uint8 v)."},"returns":{"_0":"magicValue The EIP-1271 magic value."}},"onSetAssetManager(address,bool,bytes)":{"details":"No need to check that the Account version is 3 or greater (versions with cross account reentrancy guard), since version 1 and 2 don't support the onSetAssetManager hook.","params":{"accountOwner_":"The current owner of the Arcadia Account. param status Bool indicating if the Asset Manager is enabled or disabled.","data":"Operator specific data, passed by the Account owner."}},"router()":{"returns":{"flashLoanRouter":"The address of the flash loan router contract."}},"setAccountInfo(address,address,uint256,address,bytes,bytes)":{"params":{"account_":"The contract address of the Arcadia Account to set the information for.","hookData":"Encoded data containing hook specific parameters.","initiator_":"The address of the initiator.","maxSwapFee":"The maximum fee charged on the claimed fees of the liquidity position, with 18 decimals precision.","metaData_":"Custom metadata to be stored with the account.","orderHook":"The contract address of the order hook."}},"setPauseFlag(bool)":{"params":{"paused_":"Flag indicating if the Asset Manager is paused."}},"settlementContract()":{"returns":{"cowSettlement":"The address of the settlement contract."}}},"title":"CoW Swapper for Arcadia Accounts.","version":1},"userdoc":{"kind":"user","methods":{"approve(address,address,uint256)":{"notice":"Dummy approve function required by the settlement contract. Does nothing."},"approveToken(address)":{"notice":"Approves the vaultRelayer 